---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title={''} description={'Phoenix I/O LLC: software, data and AI engineering for mission-critical systems. Small business, UEI G2VAY6MY6515, NAICS 541511.'} page="home">
<section class="page" id="p-home" data-title="Home">
  <div class="hero">
    <canvas id="flow" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="label ember">Software · Data · AI engineering</span>
      <h1 aria-label="Engineering for systems that can't fail.">Engineering for systems that <em class="rot" aria-hidden="true"><span>can't fail.</span></em></h1>
      <p class="lede">Cloud data platforms, secure applications, sub-millisecond distributed systems and AI-enabled automation, built by five principals with 20+ years of hands-on delivery each.</p>
      <div class="btns">
        <a class="btn primary" href="/contracting/">Contracting information <span class="arr">→</span></a>
        <a class="btn ghost" href="/teaming/">Partner with us</a>
      </div>
      <div class="ids" aria-label="Company identifiers">
        <span class="live">SAM <b>Active</b></span><span>UEI <b>G2VAY6MY6515</b></span><span>CAGE <b>262J4</b></span><span><b>Small Business</b></span><span>NAICS <b>541511</b></span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="metrics" aria-label="Measured results">
        <div class="m"><span class="n"><i>$</i>2M+</span><p>saved moving a Fortune 500 data platform to Snowflake</p></div>
        <div class="m"><span class="n">1,000<i>+</i></span><p>reports consolidated for a logistics and government-services contractor</p></div>
        <div class="m"><span class="n">1,500<i>×</i></span><p>faster clinical lab query, fixed with zero downtime</p></div>
        <div class="m"><span class="n"><i>&lt;</i>1ms</span><p>transaction processing supporting $1B+ in trading volume</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><div class="stack"><span class="label">What we build</span><h2>Four disciplines.<br>One senior team.</h2></div><p>From legacy migrations to lock-free trading engines, the same principals scope, architect and ship the work.</p></div>
      <div class="cols">
        <div class="col"><span class="label">01</span><h3>Data platforms and analytics</h3><p>Legacy warehouses moved to governed cloud platforms, and reporting sprawl consolidated.</p><span class="tech">Snowflake · dbt · Data Vault · Power BI</span><a class="link" href="/capabilities/">Explore →</a></div>
        <div class="col"><span class="label">02</span><h3>Applications and systems</h3><p>Secure full-stack, offline-first mobile and lock-free distributed systems.</p><span class="tech">Go · C++ · React · PostgreSQL</span><a class="link" href="/capabilities/">Explore →</a></div>
        <div class="col"><span class="label">03</span><h3>AI-enabled automation</h3><p>LLM integration and agent infrastructure, with a person approving every consequential output.</p><span class="tech">LLMs · MCP agents · human review</span><a class="link" href="/capabilities/">Explore →</a></div>
        <div class="col"><span class="label">04</span><h3>Reliability and delivery</h3><p>Observability, incident response and program management that lands on schedule.</p><span class="tech">OpenTelemetry · Datadog · Terraform</span><a class="link" href="/capabilities/">Explore →</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><div class="stack"><span class="label">Selected work</span><h2>Proven where the stakes are high.</h2></div><p>Phoenix I/O projects, and engagements our principals led at prior firms.</p></div>
      <div class="worklist">
        <a class="work" href="/projects/"><span class="k own">Phoenix I/O project</span><div><h3>MedTransport dispatch and crew platform</h3><p class="s">Dispatch, crew and fleet for medical transport, with a signed, offline-first Kotlin crew app.</p></div><span class="r">8 phases in 11 days · 112 findings fixed</span><span class="go">→</span></a>
        <a class="work" href="/projects/"><span class="k own">Phoenix I/O project</span><div><h3>High-frequency trading system</h3><p class="s">Lock-free Go and C++ across 19 venues on 2 blockchains.</p></div><span class="r">&lt;1 ms · $1B+ volume</span><span class="go">→</span></a>
        <a class="work" href="/past-performance/"><span class="k">Past performance</span><div><h3>Logistics and government-services contractor</h3><p class="s">Snowflake data lake on AWS and Power BI reporting for government services.</p></div><span class="r">$200K+/yr saved</span><span class="go">→</span></a>
        <a class="work" href="/past-performance/"><span class="k">Past performance</span><div><h3>Clinical genomics laboratory</h3><p class="s">Lab execution front end and Oracle performance work.</p></div><span class="r">1,500× query, zero downtime</span><span class="go">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><div class="stack"><span class="label">Why Phoenix I/O</span><h2>What evaluators can expect.</h2></div></div>
      <div class="principles">
        <div class="pr"><span class="label">Senior-only</span><h3>The people who scope it build it.</h3><p>No hand-off to junior staff after award.</p></div>
        <div class="pr"><span class="label">Proven savings</span><h3>$2M+ and $500K+/yr documented.</h3><p>Measured on prior engagements.</p></div>
        <div class="pr"><span class="label">Regulated data</span><h3>HIPAA, PII and audit by default.</h3><p>Compliance built in from the first sprint.</p></div>
        <div class="pr"><span class="label">AI-first</span><h3>Faster builds, human-reviewed.</h3><p>A person approves every change.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="aud">
        <a href="/contracting/"><span class="label">Contracting officers</span><h2>Company data and capability statement.</h2><p>UEI, NAICS codes, size status and a point of contact on one page.</p><span class="go">Go to Contracting →</span></a>
        <a href="/teaming/"><span class="label">Prime contractors</span><h2>Team with a senior small business.</h2><p>Small under eight NAICS codes, with work packages we own end to end.</p><span class="go">Go to Teaming →</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</section>
</Base>
